think open-image landed and shipped; the quest doc's last rung is open-image — the first Photos verb, a crop as a pure, bounded function over the decoded grid. Ungated, agent-doable, and it closes the open-image–open-image opening quest, so by Lila it is the move that finishes the started thing (the finishing edge) rather than opening a new one.
think Placed image/photos.rye in the image family (alongside qoi.rye), importing qoi.rye and tally_copy.rye — both already resolvable in image/. crop(allocator, pm, x, y, w, h): refuse EmptyRect on a zero dimension, refuse OutOfBounds when x+w or y+h reaches past the image (checked in u64 so a large coordinate cannot wrap), bound the crop by qoi_max_pixels, alloc a fresh buffer, copy_disjoint each source row's rectangle slice into the output, and return a new Pixmap. Pure by construction — the source is only read.
think Wrote a strong witness: a 6×6 image where each pixel encodes its own coordinates ((x·40, y·40, x+y, 255)) so a crop's correctness is unambiguous. Proved every cropped pixel equals its source pixel, the source is untouched (purity), the identity crop recovers the whole byte-for-byte, and — tying open-image back to open-image — a cropped image re-encodes and round-trips through the codec byte-for-byte, so a crop yields a still-open image. Empty and both edge-overrun rectangles refuse by name.
obs GREEN on the first build and run; TAME + width clean on the first check (learned from open-image/open-image — no compound asserts this time). No breach rename, no gate crossed (no network, key, or funds).
obs The opening Open Image quest is now whole end to end: open-image (codec, byte-for-byte round-trip over six chunk kinds) · open-image (content-addressed Tablecloth artifact, tampered bead refuses before a pixel is read) · open-image (down-mapped and painted through Skate, lit pixels reach the canvas) · open-image (cropped, pure and bounded). An open image module beneath the parts marketplace and the Photos app — the Lindy substrate Chapter A named.
